1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,310
What kind of fish are they?
它们是什么鱼？

2
00:00:09,310 --> 00:00:14,700
What kind of fish are they?
它们是什么鱼？

3
00:00:17,470 --> 00:00:21,280
Fish and chips has always been a favourite dish in Britain,
炸鱼和炸土豆片一直是英国人喜爱的一道菜，

4
00:00:21,300 --> 00:00:27,440
but as the oceans have been overfished, fish has become more and more expensive.
但由于海洋被过度捕捞，鱼越来越贵了。

5
00:00:27,460 --> 00:00:36,230
So it comes as a surprise to learn that giant fish are terrifying the divers on North Sea oil rigs.
因此听说北海石油钻井平台上的潜水员被巨型鱼吓得要命，令人吃惊。

6
00:00:36,530 --> 00:00:44,440
Oil rigs have to be repaired frequently and divers, who often have to work in darkness
钻井平台需要经常修理，潜水员常常得在黑暗中

7
00:00:44,460 --> 00:00:53,420
a hundred feet under water, have been frightened out of their wits by giant fish bumping into them as they work.
水下100英尺处工作，干活时撞上他们的巨型鱼把他们吓得魂不附体。

8
00:00:54,240 --> 00:00:59,610
Now they have had special cages made to protect them from these monsters.
现在他们让人做了特殊的笼子，以保护自己不受这些怪物的伤害。

9
00:00:59,630 --> 00:01:04,010
The fish are not sharks or killer whales,
这些鱼不是鲨鱼或逆戟鲸，

10
00:01:04,030 --> 00:01:11,600
but favourite eating varieties like cod and skate which grow to unnatural sizes,
而是人们爱吃的鳕鱼、鳐鱼之类，它们长到了异乎寻常的大小，

11
00:01:11,620 --> 00:01:15,420
sometimes as much as twelve feet in length.
有时长达十二英尺。

12
00:01:15,780 --> 00:01:20,030
Three factors have caused these fish to grow so large:
有三个因素使这些鱼长得如此之大：

13
00:01:20,050 --> 00:01:25,320
the warm water round the hot oil pipes under the sea;
海底热油管周围温暖的海水；

14
00:01:25,340 --> 00:01:31,130
the plentiful supply of food thrown overboard by the crews on the rigs;
平台上船员扔进海里的大量食物；

15
00:01:31,150 --> 00:01:35,600
the total absence of fishing boats around the oil rigs.
钻井平台周围根本没有渔船。

16
00:01:35,620 --> 00:01:42,450
As a result, the fish just eat and eat and grow and grow in the lovely warm water.
结果，这些鱼在温暖宜人的海水里就是不停地吃、不停地长。

17
00:01:42,470 --> 00:01:44,300
Who eats who?
到底是谁吃谁呢？
